## Conversation
User asked to stage the GLM-5.2 campaign's TorchSpec fix in this fork (branch
abatilo/improve-training-throughput) for later upstreaming; discovered during
a secretary-protocol train:infer ratio campaign in the coreweave/at repo
(recipes/training/glm_5p2_ratio_ledger.md there holds the full evidence).

## Actions
Applied the same diff as at-repo patch
docker/torchspec-amd64-ib/patches/torchspec/33d8f0f/0005-*.patch onto fork
main (exactly 33d8f0f, clean tree). Verified TorchSpec tests do not assert
the old kwargs (only the GPU integration test touches return_hidden_states,
and it calls sglang directly, not this wrapper).

## Errors & Mistakes
None in this staging step. Historically: two full experiment waves were
misled by a burst-window throughput metric before wall-clock step time
exposed the real bottleneck; both AI debaters predicted plain-sglang
slowness and were wrong (plain prefill was healthy at 50.5k tok/s).

## Dead Ends
Config-space fixes (batch size 1-32, put pool, concurrency, mem fraction,
buffers, mooncake master rpc threads): all no-ops on wall-clock — the tolist
path dominated everything.

## Hints for Future Agents
- The trainer reads tensors from Mooncake by meta_info keys; the response
  body hidden states were ALWAYS dead weight on this path.
- Bug is invisible at tp_size=1 (rank 0 owns the store); it detonates at
  tp>1 and scales with TP degree.
- Repro/verification harness: fbench (offline sgl.Engine bench inside the
  training image; needs an if __name__ == '__main__' guard because sglang
  spawns re-exec the module). a0/a3/a3b rows: plain / with-flag / without.

## Codebase Discoveries
_normalize_spec_training_params broadcasts spec_training_data_id;
CaptureHiddenMode.FULL is forced by spec_training_info alone
(forward_batch_info hunk of patches/sglang/v0.5.14/sglang.patch).

